// How this repository is deployed, in this repository.
// ADR-0097 is why this file exists rather than a set of dashboard fields, and why wrangler is a dev
// dependency of a repository that allowed four.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// It is here because there is nowhere else to put it
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// This is not a Pages project serving a folder; it is a Worker serving static assets, and the
// difference is visible from the dashboard: it offers "Cron Triggers" and "Queues", which are concepts
// of a program, and it offers **no output directory field at all**. `assets.directory` below is that
// field. The first build failed with the Cloudflare application detection logic having "been run in
// the root of a workspace instead of targeting a specific project", which is what a monorepo with no
// configuration file looks like from outside.
//
// So the two halves of a deployment now live in two places and only one of them can drift. The build
// command and the deploy command are fields of a dashboard - `pnpm run site:build` and
// `npx wrangler deploy`, both of them constants carrying no version and no path - and everything that
// is a decision is here.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What is deliberately not here
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// **No route and no custom domain.** The origin this catalogue declares is frozen into the licence
// header of every file the installer has ever written, and connecting it to a deployment that has not
// been measured would freeze whatever that deployment happens to be. It answers 403 today, and a 403
// is better than a site that is half right at the one address every installed file cites for life.
//
// **No `main`.** Nothing here runs code: an assets-only Worker needs no script, and permanent rule 1
// refuses runtime indirection in any case. What decides how a response is served is `_headers`, which
// `packages/site/served-headers.ts` derives from the endpoints and the build writes into the tree.
//
// **No `html_handling`.** Its default, `auto-trailing-slash`, serves `<contract>/index.html` at
// `<contract>/` - which is the address `linkTo` publishes, the address the sitemap carries, and the
// address a contract's licence header cites. Declaring the default would be a second statement of
// something already true.
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "toopo",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-16",

  // Written by `pnpm run site:build`, which runs from the workspace root and is not committed: a
  // rendering of the catalogue is not a contract, an implementation, a test or the evidence a run
  // produced, and `.gitignore` keeps it out.
  //
  // `pages_build_output_dir` and not `assets.directory`, and that one field is the whole migration.
  // ADR-0100 carries the measurement: the two mechanisms were deployed one variable apart, and this one
  // answers the published address with 200 and serves the `Cache-Control` `_headers` declares at the
  // address that serves the bytes. The other answered a redirect and applied the rule to the redirect.
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./packages/site/out"
}
